  "conclusion": "Both actual zero-action validation failures triggered one complete specific feedback request and the model returned substantially shorter artifacts, so feedback delivery worked. Neither revised artifact passed extraction, so execution and prediction mechanisms were not tested. The new120-line threshold rejects an otherwise definition-compliant129-line ft09 revision, while the existing all-defaults ban rejects su15 literal default10. These interface burdens must not be summarized as inability to write Python. Offline lowering these exact burdens still yields ft09 abstention and su15 projection-schema failure; neither establishes useful rules or score gain.",
